                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][u][b]A Very Classic Sudoku Game[/b][/u][/h1]\n\n[h3][b]What this game is:[/b][/h3]\nA classic sudoku game that makes you play sudoku with a classic 9 x 9 grid.\n\n[h3][b]How does it work?[/b][/h3]\nYou play on a standard sudoku game board where difficulty is gradually increased by diminishing the number of available clues.  \n\n[h3][b]How does it perform?[/b][/h3]\nVery easy to play. This is quite the standard sudoku fare. It is an uncomplicated game that will easily kill time.  You only need your mouse to play, the settings are easy to change, there are no bugs that I could see.  \n\n[h3][b]The good points:[/b][/h3]\nSimple, relaxing and inexpensive game that will provide you with many hours of play. Easy achievements to get, by completing the first 75 or 80 grids you get all Achievements in the game. Game settings are well designed, no obervable bugs. The game will run on a potato PC or a toaster. Takes less than a 225 MB of space on your HD.  Playable on the Steam Deck, but the zooming function works is a bit unwieldy.   \n\n[h3][b]The bad points:[/b][/h3]\nNot many bad points really.  I have enjoyed playing sudoku over the years and this is is quite typical, pretty standard fare for the genre.  No Steam Trading Cards. \n\n[h3][b]My take on this:[/b][/h3]\nIf you like a cheap and relaxing game, this is it. I can recommend this game for the full asking price as it is quite cheap and you will get your money's worth of playtime.  You can expect 40 to 50 hours of playing only for the first 100 grids and easily two to three times more hours by playing the bonus grids.  Recommended!",
